This distribution bundles source code and derived data from the U.S. Department
of Veterans Affairs VistA system. That material is U.S. Government work obtained
through the VA's FOIA release of VistA and is not subject to copyright in the
United States. It is redistributed here unmodified in substance, for the purpose
of verification research. The Apache License above covers Rosetta's own code; it
does not, and cannot, relicense the material below.

  data/routines/*.m
      Verbatim VistA MUMPS routines. Each file retains its original VA header
      line, including package name, version and patch level -- for example:
          GMRVPCE0 ;HIOFO/RM,FT-Data Event Driver for Vitals ;3/7/05  10:34
           ;;5.0;GEN. MED. REC. - VITALS;**8**;Oct 31, 2002

  data/fileman/dd.json.gz
      A machine-readable extract of the VistA FileMan data dictionary, derived
      from the same release.

  data/tasks/*.json
      Task, candidate and split metadata computed over the routines above.
      Derived from U.S. Government work; the derivation is Rosetta's.

  rosetta/core/m/*.m
      Rosetta's own MUMPS worker routines. These are original work under the
      Apache License, not VA material, despite sharing the .m extension.

Source of the VA material:
  https://department.va.gov/foia/foia-version-of-vista/

VistA is a system of the U.S. Department of Veterans Affairs. This project is
